        title: 'Mini Project: Full Plot Outline',
        hasImage: true,
        body:
            "For your final project, write a complete beat-by-beat plot outline for a story (short story or novel-length, your choice), using every structural element from this course. Identify your specific inciting incident, then list at least three escalating obstacles in rising action with their relative cost to the character clearly ranked, followed by a genuine midpoint turn that shifts the character's approach or understanding.\n\nOutline your low point in enough detail to show exactly what fails and what internal reckoning it forces, then outline a climax where the character actively makes the decisive choice or action themselves, directly testing the flaw or belief established earlier. Briefly describe your resolution's 'new normal,' focusing on one small, specific action that demonstrates — rather than states — your character's change.\n\nIf your story includes a subplot, note its own three-beat mini-arc and its thematic connection to the main plot. Finally, identify at least one piece of foreshadowing you'll plant early to support a later payoff. This complete outline is what you'll draft from in the prose-focused courses ahead — a strong outline here will make everything that follows dramatically easier to write.",
